=== REASONING ===

Why this design preserves ADR-015, P1-P10, and the non-AI baseline:

(1) Strategy isolation (ADR-015 §I3 — baseline intact)

    The deterministic template renderer in WeeklyDigestPage.tsx is
    UNCHANGED. Every existing section continues to render from the
    same /vehicles/{id}/weekly-digest endpoint and the same JSON
    aggregate the handler already produced. The AI surface is added
    as a new sibling component (<AIDigestNarration />) inside the
    same FadeIn block; the wrapper is a no-op when ai_mode='off' OR
    when the per-feature toggle is off, so for every off-mode user
    the page composition is byte-for-byte identical to pre-0012.

    The AI surface is gated TWICE:
      - At the React render boundary by withAiFeature (returns null)
      - At the HTTP boundary by guard.GuardedHandler.Wrap (returns 404)
    Either gate alone is sufficient; both is defense-in-depth (§I5+§I6).

(2) Registry-first wiring (P9)

    The digest-narration entry was registered with ALL RouteSet fields
    populated (Backend, Frontend, UITestIDs, JobNames, PushKinds — no
    omissions). features.CoverageOK() inspects this entry and would
    reject any field that is missing or that drifts from
    `null`-vs-`[]string{}` (the explicit-empty-array rule from the
    methodology). aigen mirrors this entry to web/src/ai/features.ts
    so the React useAiEnabled hook + withAiFeature HOC have the same
    feature ID + UI test ID as the Go side.

(3) Tool whitelist (P4 + P5 — strategy isolation)

    The strategy advertises a fixed allowedTools=["query_weekly_digest_context"]
    list. The dispatcher rejects any tool call outside that list with
    a synthetic refusal turn — a hallucinated tool name cannot reach
    a registered tool. The single allowed tool is read-only and calls
    existing Drive/Charging repositories — there is NO new SQL and NO
    write path; F4 mutation tools are not registered for this feature.

(4) Decorator chain (P5)

    The strategy resolves its provider via resolver.For(ctx, RedactionPolicy)
    AFTER the SSE stream is opened and the context is annotated with
    {subject, feature-id}. This guarantees every provider call routes
    through the locked-order decorator chain: redaction → rate → cost →
    audit → trace. The chain is identical to what chatbot-llm uses;
    no per-feature decorator was added.

(5) Redaction policy (F8 — PolicyDigest)

    PolicyDigest allows ClassVehicleName ONLY (so the narration can say
    "Roadie drove 142 mi") with Mode=ModeRedactedTags. VINs, locations,
    coordinates, addresses, IPs, phone numbers, and emails are all
    redacted before the user message reaches the provider. The
    refusal_other_vehicle golden proves the strategy refuses to discuss
    a vehicle the user does not own (the user's prompt is about a
    different VIN), so even with the allowance the model cannot be
    coerced into emitting another user's data.

(6) Off-mode contract (§I6 — 404 routes)

    POST /api/v1/ai/digests/weekly/narrate is mounted via
    g.Wrap("digest-narration", aiDigestHandler). The wrap step looks
    at settings.AIMode() FIRST; when 'off' it returns
      HTTP 404 + body `{"error":"not found"}`
    with no metadata leak (no "GUARD_BYPASSED", "feature", "strategy",
    "provider", "digest-narration" tokens). The inner handler is never
    invoked. Per-feature toggle false is treated identically to mode-off.

(7) Hidden UI (§I5)

    AIDigestNarration = withAiFeature('digest-narration', InnerSection).
    When useAiEnabled returns false, withAiFeature renders null —
    NOT a greyed-out / disabled / coming-soon card. The
    WeeklyDigestAIOff.test.tsx invariant proves the test ID
    'ai-feature-digest-narration-root' is absent from the DOM in both
    off-mode AND toggle-off configurations, with a positive control
    proving the gate is real (not a no-op trivially passing).

(8) Background job (§I12 #3)

    internal/jobs/ai_digest_weekly.RunAIDigestWeekly re-checks BOTH
    gates at execution time (not just at scheduling time) and
    fail-CLOSEs on settings-read errors (treats the read failure as
    "off" rather than "on"). When off it returns
    AIDigestWeeklyResult{Skipped:1} and never invokes a provider.
    This is a stub for the cron — actual fan-out is deferred to a
    future slice; the slot exists so the registry's JobNames is not
    a lie.

(9) Push kind metadata (§I12 #2)

    "ai_digest_ready" is registered in the RouteSet so when the
    push fan-out worker is added later it can filter by kind AND
    by recipient ai_mode at delivery time. No push is produced by
    this slice (the cron is a stub) so there is no behavior to
    test beyond the metadata invariant; future slices will exercise
    the actual filter.

(10) Allowed-files boundary

    Every modified or new file is within the slice prompt's allowed
    list (see === CHANGES ===). web/src/ai/features.ts is the
    aigen-generated mirror — it MUST be regenerated after registry
    edits so aigen --check passes; this is the established practice
    from F0/F2/0011 and is implicitly allowed by the rule that
    aivet/aigen must succeed in the gate.

